{"schema":2,"id":"KH0074","investigatorId":"AS063","provenance":null,"discoveredBy":null,"discoveredOn":null,"collection":{"name":"Óscar Núñez del Prado","city":"Cuzco","country":"Peru"},"notes":"1. Construction note: This is two quipus tied together. Both main cords and all pendant cords are W. The twisted end of the main cord A is bent back and slipped through the strands of itself forming a closed loop from which P1 and P2 are suspended. The other end of main cord A is tied around main cord B. (See Ascher notes page 358.) 2. This quipu is associated with AS059-AS067. See discussion under AS059. 3. By spacing, there are 6 groups. On part A there are groups of 2,3,4 pendants, and on part B there are 3 groups of 8 pendants each. 4. The pendants can be segregated into those whose values are 15 or less and those that are greater than 18 as follows: 5. Pendants 1 and 2, set off in a special loop, have the values 18 and 7. These values are significant in that all values greater than 18 that appear on the quipu are multiples of 18 or of 7. The multiples of each that appear are 18,36,5","primaryCord":{"length":21,"color":"W","beginning":"T","termination":"K","notes":""},"cords":[{"parent":null,"level":1,"up":false,"position":7.0,"positionRecorded":false,"length":34,"color":"W","colorOperator":null,"color2":null,"termination":"K","twist":null,"attachment":null,"fiber":null,"group":1,"knots":[{"position":11,"type":"S","count":1,"value":10,"direction":null},{"position":21,"type":"L","count":1,"value":8,"direction":null}],"note":""},{"parent":null,"level":1,"up":false,"position":7.5,"positionRecorded":false,"length":43,"color":"W","colorOperator":null,"color2":null,"termination":"K","twist":null,"attachment":null,"fiber":null,"group":1,"knots":[{"position":19,"type":"L","count":1,"value":300,"direction":null},{"position":26,"type":"L","count":1,"value":44,"direction":null}],"note":""},{"parent":null,"level":1,"up":false,"position":3.0,"positionRecorded":true,"length":39.5,"co